N2  - Alzheimer′s disease (AD) is one of the most common type of dementia, which is characterized by a progressive decline in cognitive function, accompanied by abnormal behavior, and eventual loss of daily living ability. Unfortunately, there is currently no specific drug to treat or reverse the pathological progression of AD. Therefore, the early identification and accurate assessment of AD based on the individualized level are the current research hotspots. Virtual reality (VR) technology has been increasingly applied in AD research in recent years due to its advantages of repeatability, timely feedback, controllable stimulation, and environmental safety. This paper briefly reviews the research progress of VR in the assessment of the specific cognitive function in the AD spectrum population and explores the potential of VR in the accurate assessment of AD.
