N2  - The proceedings contain 419 papers. The topics discussed include: improving episodic future thinking (EFT) in children with ADHD through VR game-based training; obtaining a clinical research master’s degree among paradigm shifts: is it worth it; a community-based approach to promoting brain health and research engagement among black refugees; cachexia underdiagnosis and diagnostic delay in head and neck cancer: insights from EHR weight data; locked out twice: how incarceration history shapes healthcare access for adults with mental illness; antibacterial effects of the MEK1/2 inhibitor ATR-002 on Staphylococcus aureus; why is the concept of translational science so hard to define and apply?; virtual expansion and impact of team science training: a mixed methods evaluation across the Washington, Wyoming, Alaska, Montana, Idaho (WWAMI) region; COMPASS: comprehensive multimodal performance assessment for safe vascular AI systems using Curie8, an LLM-based medical imaging data pipeline; gynecologic surgeon agreement and accuracy in describing endometriotic lesions; synthetic data generation using generative AI to support biomedical innovation: a health policy perspective; integrating pathology reports into multimodal machine learning models to predict thyroid cancer recurrence; validation of clinical vignettes for a translational study evaluating ChatGPT’s diagnostic support in adolescent and young adults’ mental health; and benchmarking automated segmentation tools for white matter hyperintensities quantification to inform stroke and dementia risk stratification.
