N2  - The proceedings contain 703 papers. The topics discussed include: co-producing a survey on prospective acceptability of neuromodulation for mental health conditions with lived experience experts; systematic review: are table-top roleplaying games a useful therapeutic tool for people with neurodiversity?; VR for mental health interventions at home: feasibility and guiding principles for success; multi-parametric cerebellar neuroimaging in subjective cognitive decline as predictors of cognitive alterations in Alzheimer's spectrum; effect of the COVID-19 pandemic and isolation measures on the mental health well-being of sixth form grammar school students in Cumbria; COVID-19 vaccine and active infection associated neuropsychiatric manifestations in an adolescent: a literature review; and impact of Werther effect exerted by social media on individuals presenting with deliberate self-harm (DSH) to a tertiary care hospital in Sri Lanka.
