N2  - The proceedings contain 110 papers. The topics discussed include: cost-effectiveness analysis of atropine for the prevention of myopia progression in children; E-nergEYEze, an E-health intervention to reduce fatigue in adults with visual impairment: outcomes of an economic evaluation alongside a randomized controlled trial; how the digital revolution contributes to the myopia epidemic; to understand the relationship between self- reported birth measures and (1) vision- related quality of life (VR- QoL) and (2) the presence of myopia in adults in the general population; the sense and nonsense of patient- reported outcome measures - in search of the Dutch ophthalmological society's standpoint; and temporal dynamics of retinal vascular parameters in preclinical Alzheimer's disease.
