N2  - The proceedings contain 27 papers. The topics discussed include: metacognition in mci: a research proposal on assessing the efficacy of a metacognitive intervention; exploring modeling analogies between living and non-living systems; cognitive training in community dwelling older adults via a commercial video game and an adaptation of the virtual reality platform FitForAll: comparison of the two intervention programs; brief review and research proposal about mind, dimensia, sleep and MCI; creating and sustaining a social health care ecosystem: the case of LLM care services in Greece; out-of-class vs. classroom-based learning: which is the best way to master a foreign language?; and development and testing of a monitoring system assisting patients with mild cognitive impairment (MCI) using new technologies in the frame of the European project INLIFE.
