N2  - Objective: To review the development in researches about vascular cognitive impairment (VCI), so as to prevent and treat VCI and elevate the quality of life in VCI patients. Data Source: A computer-based search was conducted in Wanfang database for the Chinese articles about VCI between January 2002 and January 2007 by using the key words of "vascular cognitive impairment, virtual reality, errorless learning, telerehabilitation". Meanwhile, the relevant English articles between January 1998 and January 2007 were searched in Pubmed with the identical key words published in English. Study Selection: Over 100 articles were collected firstly, and those related to VCI were selected. Data Extraction: Totally 34 relevant articles were selected, which were classified, including 22 articles about diagnosis of VCI and 12 articles about rehabilitation treatment of VCI patients. Data Synthesis: Through the imaging examinations of magnetic resonance blood perfusion weighted imaging, magnetic resonance spectroscopy, diffusion-weighted imaging, radioactive nuclide functional imaging and so on, the patients of VCI all appear different extents of abnormality. The application of neuropsychology test, virtual reality and computer aided technique can survey extremely impalpable cognitive impairment of patients, so they can get early diagnosis and treatment as to prevent or postpone the development dementia. The application of errorless learning and telerehabilitation can favorably improve the cognitive impairment and functional activity of patients. Conclusion: VCI is crucial for the activity of daily life in the patients, whose quality of life can be improved by early prevention, diagnosis and rehabilitation.
